{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['knowledge']=[{\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"6420ecc11ae840028bf3e70220f5fd17-knowledge-1\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A configuration that a node holds only in its log can be restored to that node's in-memory state by four paths, of which only one is in-protocol and none of which works on a running node with a complete log: a later configuration entry replicated by a correctly configured leader (appendEntries processes new configuration entries); an operator restart with RestoreCommittedLogs disabled; RecoverCluster on the stopped node with the configuration supplied, which writes a snapshot carrying it and truncates the log so the next NewRaft restores it from the snapshot; and an installed snapshot, whose metadata carries the configuration, although a leader sends a snapshot only to a follower that lacks already-compacted entries, which such a node does not. Live bootstrap on the running node does not repair it, because it refuses with ErrCantBootstrap whenever state exists. Where every voter restarts with the flag and no covering snapshot, the in-protocol path needs a leader that the empty configuration prevents from being elected, so the cluster stays unavailable until an operator acts.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore and configuration entries inside the replayed committed prefix; the in-protocol and snapshot paths are observed with a four-voter cluster in which a stale node is a minority, the no-repair case with three voters all restarted at once, and the operator paths with a single-voter cluster in the empty-configuration state.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"append_new_entries\\\",\\\"snapshot_install_config\\\",\\\"bootstrap_refusal\\\",\\\"recover_cluster\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"6d6abaf163524e64878c6c9810de2461\\\":[5],\\\"4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a\\\":[1],\\\"0440f054115e44f4a0234c7a4ef67150\\\":[1,2]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"Statement corrected and extended: the previous revision enumerated exactly three repair paths and did not mention RecoverCluster. The operator-recovery execution (receipt 0440f054115e44f4a0234c7a4ef67150) established a fourth path — RecoverCluster on a stopped node with the configuration supplied — and a path that explicitly does not work, live bootstrap on the running node, which refuses with ErrCantBootstrap while leaving the configuration empty, as well as the earlier reachability boundary that no snapshot is sent to a node whose log is complete. The conditions and source list are extended accordingly; earlier executions and the claims they support are unchanged.\\\"\n}]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
